WEBVTT

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:05.270
M.J.B.K., show me your meaning.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:08.500
Dan! Dan! Dan!

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.570
"Sever"

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.660
Da-Dan!

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:14.570
What's with these guys?
When did they get here?

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.950
What the hell? It won't connect.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.950
"Connecting..."

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:23.080
"Could not connect to network. Either the

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:23.080
server is busy, or the page could not be found.

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:23.080
Set up another connection or wait some

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:23.080
time before attempting to access again."

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:26.920
The internet and cellphones have all been disconnected?

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.790
That's a deathblow for modern society.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:34.100
The power to sever connections?
To think it could prevent our Gattai...

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.530
The bonds that tie people together...

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.070
Do you really think they can be severed so easily?

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:41.100
Kaibuki...

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.590
Come.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.210
"Bond"

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.650
We can do it like this.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.380
Sousei Gattai.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:58.120
Shout! Aquarion!

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:12.820
"Moonbind"

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.770
Moonbind!

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:16.910
"Moonbind"

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:20.410
Dan! Dan!

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:23.170
Dan!

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.980
"Bond"

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.290
I've been waiting... for that voice.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.990
Through the swelling of the "bond" kanji,

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:38.430
people and information that would not normally be connected now are.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.660
"Bond"

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.630
Huh? What's going on here?

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:43.360
There's data flowing in from all sorts of places.

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:45.870
Huh?

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.940
Hey, what's with this?
They're suddenly mad about something.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:51.440
"Aim for Nanseki High!!"

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:51.800
My folks are, too.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.370
Huh?

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:02.480
This place is...

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.690
Master Sougon!

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.350
That's him...

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.820
In being connected,

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.360
a chain of hatred between people is formed.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.360
It will eat away at the word,

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:17.200
and become the basis for a new M.J.B.K.

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:23.240
Rejoice. I shall now set you free.

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:29.070
Master Sougon!

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:34.810
That's right. I'll be the one to bring Maia back.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.020
Mr. Hayashi?

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:39.690
I've marked it and made corrections for you.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:42.890
Honestly, the logic is a mess.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:46.900
I'd have to give this design a failing mark.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.330
Though the concept isn't bad.

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:50.330
Then...

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:54.540
Got her perfectly tuned.
All dressed up with the new system, too.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.940
She's waiting for you.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.910
Maia...

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:05.210
Master Sougon... Why won't you say anything to me?

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:07.350
Face forward. It's coming.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:15.350
En. En. En. En. En. En.
En. En. En. En. En. En. En!

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:21.960
"Kebachi: This is pretty lame. lol

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:21.960
Prince Mayo: I hate seeing pricks like

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:21.960
