00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:20.430
Yes, ma'am.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:23.570
Word corrosion rate has exceeded 80%!

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:27.170
At this rate, the concept of flame will be extinguished!

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:29.080
Is there anything we can do?

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:36.280
These fools spew malice,

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.450
"Kebachi: This is pretty lame. lol

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.450
Prince Mayo: I hate seeing pricks like

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.450
him who've got it made screw around.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.450
I hope his videos die in a fire.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.450
Uji: Don't force us to watch

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.450
your boring shit you scrub."

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:35.650
"tsutstsu: Stealing someone

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:35.650
else's pet is a crime.

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:35.650
tsutstsu: Do you know how it feels

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:35.650
to have a family member stolen? I hope

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:35.650
you feel the full weight of the law."

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:36.450
"Gold: Found his real name and address!"

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:41.660
yet mistakenly believe themselves safe from it.

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:37.450
"Ouchi: A pedo and a liar?

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:37.450
This guy's beyond help.

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:37.450
fU-san: That came back and

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:37.450
bit him hard. My condolences.

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:37.450
D ran: This is what passes for a senator?"

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:39.450
"Yoshinori Akasaka Official Shigotosuki:

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:39.450
So desperate. Get lost.

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:39.450
Bihada-<i>san</i>: I hope he dies

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:39.450
an awful death. For real.

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:39.450
Kyotoikitai: The only way out now is suicide."

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:44.790
Soon, they shall learn.

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:47.330
That the blade of the written word, when pointed at another,

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:50.260
can cut both ways.

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:51.930
Die. Die.

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:54.030
Get wrecked, you moron!

00:12:51.970 --> 00:12:54.300
"I hope you die."

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:03.810
Save us!

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:09.980
The flames won't go out! Why?!

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:14.860
Hey, what are we spraying water on?

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:16.660
What do you mean, what?

00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:18.860
What is that?

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:23.130
Humans understand all phenomena through writing and words.

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:25.700
And so, should those be lost,

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:28.870
will humans still recognize those things?

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:30.840
The answer is nay.

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:33.670
When the concept of flame vanishes,

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:38.310
people will be unable to comprehend what is burning in front of them,

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:41.020
and will lose any means of dealing with it.

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:44.350
And once all the kanji in a space are consumed

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:47.350
and the M.J.B.K. has extinguished their concept,

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:49.920
it will be released into the Logos World,

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:54.560
giving birth to the next M.J.B.K., which will in turn attack another kanji.

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:59.370
When all kanji have lost their concepts to that chain,

00:13:59.370 --> 00:14:02.530
modern society will be extinguished.

00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:09.210
Corrosion rate is 90%. It's too late...

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:12.780
Commander's order 4685... Shirobaco.

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:14.610
Command acknowledged.

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:20.940
Commander!

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:25.290
All staff, evacuate.

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:28.130
Deava will now abandon this base.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:31.930
Evacuate? What good is running going to do?
At this rate, the damages will--

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:33.730
They will not keep piling up.

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:35.900
I'm going to go put a stop to that.

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:40.210
I'll go into the Wordspace with the stone monument.

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:41.700
Commander...

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:47.620
The existence of this monument, in and of itself,

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:50.080
acts as a countermeasure against the Book of Verbalism.

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:52.790
If the monument is brought into Wordspace,

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:57.660
the space will close at once, preventing the loss of its concept.

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:00.930
I-It closes... the space?

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:04.090
Wh-What about Akira and the others inside it?

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:08.340
If they're inside Aquarion, protected by Verbalism Ability,

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:12.940
it might be possible for them to make it back here.

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:15.440
M-Might be possible?

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:17.180
I'll take a Vector.

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:20.250
If all I'm doing is launching into the space,

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:22.920
even my piloting ability should be enough.

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:25.020
Shoko, I'm counting on you for support.

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:29.820
Wait! If you go in there, the Vector's going to melt, right?!

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:32.920
Maybe I should put on sunscreen.

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:38.330
I can't believe I'm hearing this!
You can't just do whatever suits you!

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:41.300
Once the space opens, a powerful backdraft

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:44.200
will turn the entire base into a hot zone.

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:46.870
Kento, you lead the evacuation.

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:48.340
Sakurako...

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:50.040
Listen to me!

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:51.780
Are you going to make us run away by ourselves?

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:54.650
How are we supposed to get by from here on without you?

00:15:54.650 --> 00:15:56.680
There'll be more M.J.B.K.s, right?

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:59.220
If you don't survive now...

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:01.350
...you won't have a later to worry about!

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:19.640
What is this?

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:21.310
Don't tell me...

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:23.910
...it's refusing...

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:25.980
...to save us...

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:28.750
To save foolish humans...

00:16:32.390 --> 00:16:35.860
In the end, I can't do anything.

00:16:35.860 --> 00:16:37.480
I'm terrible.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:46.200
Subete is in that Vector.

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:50.040
Then is this Master Sougon's will?

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:52.340
It can't...

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:57.900
Master Sougon... What should I have done?

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:04.050
That's the limit. You've merged with the M.J.B.K. too much.

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:05.450
Withdraw.

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:08.920
Withdraw? What are you saying, Mr. Hayashi?

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:12.430
I still haven't accomplished my objective.

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:15.920
If you don't, the M.J.B.K. will devour that concept.

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:21.540
My objective...

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:26.270
Huh? What is an objective again?

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:28.070
Oh, who cares?

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:35.320
Humans, through malice, will close the curtain on their own civilization.

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:38.410
This is not a dissatisfying conclusion.

00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:43.490
Kaibuki...

00:18:29.470 --> 00:18:31.670
It's not entirely clear why,

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:33.770
but the damage has stopped spreading.

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:36.280
The situation is subsiding in all areas.

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:37.680
Why?

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:42.850
Why do you save the fools struck by their own malice?

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:45.880
Why... are you...?

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:49.960
Because I can hear...

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:51.690
...their voices!

00:18:53.030 --> 00:18:57.060
I remember now! The red Vector!

00:18:57.060 --> 00:19:02.070
You stole my precious Maia from me!

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:06.060
The voices... seeking salvation!

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:12.340
What?

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:15.640
You're...

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:18.690
By wreathing them in flame,

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:22.260
the Vectors are protected from the heat around them?

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:23.920
Is that possible...?

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:28.400
I'm fine with being terrible.

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:31.400
Right now, you're all I have.

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:34.230
Kaibuki...

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:35.860
Akira.

00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:42.580
Sousei... Gattai...

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:48.520
Dance! Aquarion!

00:19:57.020 --> 00:19:58.360
"Zai [Sin]"

00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:58.850
Zai.

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:06.270
Let me show you the true flames of will!

00:20:05.070 --> 00:20:06.460
"Flame"

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:20.940
Heat Haze Dance!

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:20.110
"Heat Haze Dance"

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:45.730
Red Vector!

00:20:47.570 --> 00:20:49.130
Maia...

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:53.450
I... I'm not...! I...!

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:56.320
For as long as there are voices that seek it,

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:55.520
"Voice"

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:58.780
I will bring salvation to everything!

00:20:56.980 --> 00:20:58.090
"Save"

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:03.520
For I am...

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:08.600
"Savior"

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:08.620
...the savior!

00:21:13.930 --> 00:21:15.600
"Flame"

00:21:21.110 --> 00:21:23.540
You even saved me?

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:28.280
"Akira Kaibuki"

00:21:25.310 --> 00:21:27.780
Akira... Kaibuki?

00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:33.220
"Subete Kenzaki"

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:30.820
Subete Kenzaki.

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:39.550
Kai... Kaibuki!

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:48.500
Subete...

00:21:54.840 --> 00:21:59.250
How was your first flight?

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:00.740
Awful.

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:04.920
I won't forget this...

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:06.980
...Akira Kaibuki.

00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:12.890
Fate has gone into motion.

00:22:12.890 --> 00:22:16.560
How will this world appear in your eyes...

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:19.830
...O Nesta?

00:22:37.420 --> 00:22:40.890
<i>Je-Je t'aime communication</i>

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:50.890
<i>Oh, you aren't making a bit of</i> <i>eye contact with me while you talk</i>

00:22:50.930 --> 00:23:00.140
<i>Are you texting some far-off</i> <i>neighboring world or something?</i>

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:05.270
<i>Because this isn't communication at all</i>

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:13.750
<i>You'd at least understand that much</i>

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:19.760
<i>even if the times suddenly changed, right?</i>

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:23.760
<i>Give me je t'aime communication sometimes</i>

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:27.170
<i>Look at me, answer me, and tell me</i>

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:33.670
<i>I mean, this is practically</i> <i>like talking to a computer</i>

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:36.680
<i>A-Adieu application</i>

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:43.320
<i>Even if it means staying lonely</i> <i>in my heart, if it'll connect us</i>

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:49.690
<i>then, please, at least show</i> <i>your smile to me alone</i>

00:23:50.990 --> 00:23:55.330
"Cicada"

00:23:52.760 --> 00:23:55.430
--What's wrong?
--There's a gigantic cicada in the shop!

00:23:55.430 --> 00:23:57.660
I must save all things equally, for I am...

00:23:57.660 --> 00:23:59.770
Enough of that! Do something!

00:23:59.770 --> 00:24:00.930
H-He caught it!

00:24:00.930 --> 00:24:02.970
Our savior!

00:24:02.970 --> 00:24:04.600
What a relief.

00:24:04.600 --> 00:24:06.040
Next time: Episode 8.

00:24:05.170 --> 00:24:09.040
"Episode 8: Pierce It! The Insect Part"

00:24:06.040 --> 00:24:08.980
"Pierce It! The Insect Part."

00:24:08.980 --> 00:24:10.840
Wait, an insect?!
